-- Baseline data for a fresh database, in the official Remix demo's seed style.
-- Statements are idempotent (`insert or ignore` on every primary or unique key), so the seed
-- is safe to run against an already-seeded database: `remix db seed` and `remix db reset
-- --force` both re-run it. The password hash is pbkdf2_sha256 (see app/data/password.ts):
--   demo@meridian.test   demo-password
--
-- The seeded issued documents carry their stored PDF artifacts: those bytes are the exact
-- renderInvoicePdf() output for these rows. If the seed rows or the renderer ever change,
-- regenerate them with the recipe in docs/manual-checks/2026-11-19-seed-baseline-and-db-scripts.md
-- and delete the dev database (ADR-0003: never migrate a stale one).

-- The demo User, its credentials, the Organization, and the owner membership.

